  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will begin to solve quadratic equations by reasoning about what values would make the equations true and by using structure in the equations. You will explore in depth the idea that some quadratic equations have two solutions. </para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to: </para>
<list>
  <item> Find solutions to quadratic equations by reasoning about the values that make the equation true. </item>
  <item> Explain that quadratic equations may have one or two solutions. </item>
  <item> Implement the square root property. </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 8.3.1: Determining the Number of Solutions </item>
  <item> 8.3.2: Recognizing Pairs of Solutions </item>
  <list>
    <item> 8.3.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 8.3.2: Additional Resources  </item>
  </list>
  <item> 8.3.3: Solving More Complex Quadratic Equations </item>
  <list>
    <item> 8.3.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 8.3.3: Additional Resources  </item>
  </list>
  <item> 8.3.4: Finding the Solutions </item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 8.3.5: Practice </item>
  <item> 8.3.6: Lesson Summary </item>
</list></section>
</content>
